# UI Consistency Rules - Shadcn Design System

## 🎯 Core Principles

### 1. Always Use Shadcn Variables
- **NEVER** use hardcoded colors like `text-blue-600`, `bg-red-100`, or `border-green-200`
- **ALWAYS** use shadcn CSS variables from `globals.css`
- **EXCEPTION**: Email components may use specific Tailwind colors for email client compatibility

### 2. Consistent Component Usage
- **AVOID** creating custom styled components that duplicate existing shadcn/ui functionality
- **ALWAYS** check if a shadcn component exists before creating custom alternatives
- **REUSE** existing components and extend them with proper variants

### 3. Icon Color Patterns
- **NEVER** use colored icons with arbitrary colors
- **ALWAYS** use foreground colors that match their background context
- Icons should inherit appropriate contrast colors

## 🎨 Color System Guidelines

### Primary Color Usage
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Use shadcn variables
<div className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground">
  <Shield className="text-primary-foreground" />
</div>

// ❌ WRONG: Hardcoded colors
<div className="bg-blue-600 text-white">
  <Shield className="text-white" />
</div>
```

### Background & Foreground Pairs
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Proper contrast pairs
bg-background + text-foreground
bg-primary + text-primary-foreground  
bg-secondary + text-secondary-foreground
bg-destructive + text-destructive-foreground
bg-muted + text-muted-foreground
bg-accent + text-accent-foreground
bg-card + text-card-foreground
bg-popover + text-popover-foreground

// ❌ WRONG: Mismatched pairs
bg-primary + text-white
bg-card + text-gray-900
```

### Semantic Color Usage
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Semantic meaning
text-muted-foreground    // For less important text
text-destructive         // For errors/danger
border-input            // For form inputs
ring-ring               // For focus states

// ❌ WRONG: Arbitrary semantic colors
text-gray-500
text-red-600
border-blue-200
```

## 🏷️ Badge Component Patterns

### Standard Badge Variants
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Use predefined variants
<Badge variant="default">Primary action</Badge>
<Badge variant="secondary">Secondary info</Badge>
<Badge variant="destructive">Error state</Badge>
<Badge variant="outline">Neutral state</Badge>

// ❌ WRONG: Custom colored badges
<Badge className="bg-blue-100 text-blue-700">Custom</Badge>
<Badge className="border-green-200 text-green-600">Status</Badge>
```

### Status Badge Patterns
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Semantic status badges
const getStatusBadge = (status: string) => {
  switch (status) {
    case "pending":
      return <Badge variant="secondary">Pending</Badge>;
    case "processing": 
      return <Badge variant="default">Processing</Badge>;
    case "completed":
      return <Badge variant="outline" className="border-green-600 text-green-600 dark:border-green-400 dark:text-green-400">Completed</Badge>;
    case "cancelled":
      return <Badge variant="destructive">Cancelled</Badge>;
  }
};

// ❌ WRONG: Hardcoded status colors
<Badge className="bg-yellow-100 text-yellow-700">Processing</Badge>
<Badge className="bg-red-100 text-red-700">Error</Badge>
```

## 🎭 Icon Guidelines

### Icon Color Inheritance
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Icons inherit from context
<Badge variant="primary">
  <CheckIcon className="text-primary-foreground" />
  Success
</Badge>

<div className="text-muted-foreground">
  <InfoIcon className="text-current" />
  Additional info
</div>

// ❌ WRONG: Hardcoded icon colors
<CheckIcon className="text-green-600" />
<AlertIcon className="text-red-500" />
```

### Icon Size Consistency
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Consistent icon sizes
<Icon className="h-4 w-4" />     // Small icons in text
<Icon className="h-5 w-5" />     // Medium icons in buttons
<Icon className="h-6 w-6" />     // Large icons in cards

// ❌ WRONG: Random icon sizes
<Icon className="w-3 h-3" />
<Icon className="size-7" />
```

## 🏗️ Component Architecture

### Avatar Components
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Use shadcn variables
<div className="bg-primary rounded-full">
  <span className="text-primary-foreground">{initials}</span>
</div>

// ❌ WRONG: Hardcoded gradients
<div className="bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-600 to-purple-600">
  <span className="text-white">{initials}</span>
</div>
```

### Card Components
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Use card variants
<Card className="bg-card">
  <CardHeader>
    <div className="bg-primary/10 rounded-lg">
      <Icon className="text-primary" />
    </div>
  </CardHeader>
</Card>

// ❌ WRONG: Custom card styling
<Card className="bg-white/80 dark:bg-gray-800/80 border-0">
  <div className="bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/20">
    <Icon className="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400" />
  </div>
</Card>
```

### Button Consistency
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Use button variants
<Button variant="default">Primary Action</Button>
<Button variant="outline">Secondary Action</Button>
<Button variant="destructive">Delete</Button>
<Button variant="ghost">Subtle Action</Button>

// ❌ WRONG: Custom button styling
<Button className="bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white">
  Custom Button
</Button>
```

## 📱 Responsive & Theme Patterns

### Theme-Aware Styling
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Let shadcn handle dark mode
<div className="bg-background text-foreground">
  <p className="text-muted-foreground">Description</p>
</div>

// ❌ WRONG: Manual dark mode classes
<div className="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">
  <p className="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Description</p>
</div>
```

### Background Patterns
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Semantic backgrounds
bg-background      // Main page background
bg-card           // Card backgrounds  
bg-muted/30       // Subtle section backgrounds
bg-accent/50      // Highlighted areas

// ❌ WRONG: Hardcoded backgrounds
bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 via-white to-indigo-50
bg-white/80 dark:bg-gray-900/80
```

## 🔧 Migration Patterns

### From Hardcoded to Shadcn Variables
```tsx
// Migration example:
// BEFORE
className="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100"
className="bg-blue-600 text-white"
className="border-green-200 text-green-700"

// AFTER  
className="text-foreground"
className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground"
className="border-green-600 text-green-600 dark:border-green-400 dark:text-green-400"
```

### Status Color Migration
```tsx
// BEFORE: Hardcoded status colors
const statusColors = {
  success: "text-green-600 bg-green-100",
  warning: "text-yellow-600 bg-yellow-100", 
  error: "text-red-600 bg-red-100"
};

// AFTER: Semantic variants
const getStatusVariant = (status) => {
  switch (status) {
    case "success": return "outline" + " border-green-600 text-green-600";
    case "warning": return "secondary";
    case "error": return "destructive";
  }
};
```

## ✅ Checklist for New Components

Before creating/modifying any UI component:

- [ ] Does a similar shadcn component already exist?
- [ ] Are you using shadcn CSS variables instead of hardcoded colors?
- [ ] Do icons use appropriate foreground colors?
- [ ] Are color pairs semantically correct (bg + text)?
- [ ] Will this work in both light and dark themes?
- [ ] Are you using consistent badge/button variants?
- [ ] Does the component follow the established patterns?

## 🚫 Common Anti-Patterns to Avoid

```tsx
// ❌ NEVER do these:
className="text-blue-600"                    // Use text-primary
className="bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-600"   // Use bg-primary  
className="border-green-200"                 // Use semantic borders
style={{ color: BRAND_CONFIG.colors.text }} // Use CSS variables
className="hover:bg-blue-700"                // Use variant hover states
className="dark:bg-gray-800"                 // Let shadcn handle themes
```

## 📝 Quick Reference

### Most Common Replacements
```tsx
// Text Colors
text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100  →  text-foreground
text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400  →  text-muted-foreground
text-blue-600                     →  text-primary
text-red-600                      →  text-destructive

// Background Colors  
bg-white dark:bg-gray-900         →  bg-background
bg-gray-50                        →  bg-muted/30
bg-blue-600                       →  bg-primary
bg-red-600                        →  bg-destructive

// Borders
border-gray-200                   →  border-border
border-blue-600                   →  border-primary
```

---

**Remember**: Consistency is key. When in doubt, check existing shadcn components and follow their patterns. Always prioritize semantic meaning over visual appearance.